course: dictionary
lesson: 2700
title: Digest: food, ideas and summaries
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word digest has three meanings, so context decides which one you need. Ask: what is being digested, food, ideas or a summary? «Spotted hyenas have some of the strongest bites of any mammal and can crush and digest bones.» Here digest means breaking food down inside the body.
explain: «Most adult cats cannot digest milk sugar well and can get an upset tummy.» The body cannot break that sugar down properly, so the cat's tummy gets upset. Teachers also use digest in a different way: they give pupils time to digest new ideas, which means to think about them carefully until they make sense.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Mia needs time to digest what she has learned» still makes sense when you read it as think about it until you understand. Digest can also be a noun, a digest, which is a short summary of news or writing.
fact: To digest food means to break it down in the stomach and intestines so the body can use it for energy and growth.
fact: To digest information means to think about it carefully until you understand it.
fact: «Digest» is a verb: digest, digests, digested, digesting. «A digest» (said DY-jest) is a noun for a short summary.
fact: «Hard to digest» means difficult for the body to break down, and «digestive system» means the whole set of body parts that break food down.
fact: Fibre helps digestion, and «chewing gum is not digested» at all: it passes through the body in a few days.
exercise: «Trillions of microbes live in your gut helping to digest food.» What does digest mean here? | *To break down food so the body can use it | To cook food in hot water | To swallow food quickly without chewing | To throw food away
exercise: Mia says, «I need time to digest what the teacher said.» What does digest mean? | *To think about it carefully until you understand | To forget it completely | To eat it all up
exercise: A short summary of news or writing is called a... | digestive | digesting | *digest | digester
test: «Swallowed chewing gum is not digested but passes through in a few days.» What does this tell us? | Gum turns into energy for the body | The body breaks gum down within an hour | *The body cannot break gum down | Gum is food for the stomach
test: Dad reads a digest of the news each morning. What is a digest? | *A short summary of news or writing | To chew slowly | A large meal | A kind of stomach
exam: Which phrase uses digest to mean think about it until you understand? | *digest the news | digest food | digestive system | hard to digest
